From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Tue, 17 Sep 2024 04:43:58 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7915: fix single SKU power limits

The patch "wifi: mt76: mt7996: support txpower backoff table" widens
the path power limits for mt799x, so the other chips parse the path
tables with their own smaller sizes again. The path table is on only
if the device tree has a path entry for a channel. In PSD countries
the driver, not the firmware, compensates the OFDM limits with the
limits of the channel width, and Canada joins the list of PSD
countries.

The driver sends the single SKU tables each time it enables the SKU
limits: at radio start, after a full reset, after a change of country
or DFS region, and in testmode. A failed table upload goes back to the
caller after both enables are sent, so that the enables still match
the current settings. After a country change or a full reset it also
sends the LPI command again when LPI is on: the PSD limit of that
command follows the country, and the firmware reload drops the LPI
state, which hostapd sends only at interface setup. Without these
updates, a running radio keeps the limits of the old country. Each
band compares the country with the one it applied last, because
cfg80211 calls the notifier once for each wiphy of the device. The
updates and the txpower vendor command hold the device mutex, so that
the radio cannot stop or change its channel during the upload and two
LPI commands cannot interleave. The 6 GHz LPI flags move from the
device to the phy, so a vendor command on one band does not change the
other bands.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
